		{"id":"group_terraform","type":"group","x":-800,"y":240,"width":500,"height":680,"color":"2","label":"🏗️ Terraform Senior Architecture Cheat Sheet"},
		{"id":"group_sre_pitch","type":"group","x":300,"y":240,"width":500,"height":680,"color":"1","label":"🚒 SRE Incident Triage & Final Interview Pitch"},
		{"id":"legend_node","type":"text","text":"### 🎨 Status & Color Legend\n- **Default (No Color)**: To Learn\n- **Yellow (Color 3)**: In Progress\n- **Orange (Color 2)**: Review/Apply\n- **Green (Color 4)**: Mastered","x":-800,"y":-720,"width":380,"height":180},
		{"id":"banner_node","type":"text","text":"# 🔴 SME Level 2 Technical Round\n**Role:** Senior Cloud DevOps Engineer\n**Target:** Technical SME Round\n**Platform:** RapidResponse SaaS | Chennai\n**Focus:** Terraform, Python, GHA vs Argo, CI/CD, Bots","x":-380,"y":-720,"width":460,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"py_basics","type":"text","text":"### [[5. Python ETL & Scripting Mastery#python-basics-refresher-for-devops--cloud-interviews|1. Python Data Structures & Core Idioms]]\n- **Big-O Lookups:** `set` & `dict` are **O(1) instant hash lookup**. Never do `if x in list` (O(N) slow)!\n- **Defensive Parsing:** Always use `dict.get(\"key\", default)` — prevents crashing on `KeyError`.\n- **Context Managers:** `with open(\"logs.json\", \"r\") as f:` guarantees file descriptor closure even on exceptions.\n- **List Comprehensions:** `[int(x) for x in codes if int(x) >= 500]` for clean, Pythonic filtering.\n- **`defaultdict`:** `defaultdict(lambda: {\"count\": 0})` avoids `if key not in dict` checks.","x":-770,"y":-420,"width":700,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"py_etl","type":"text","text":"### [[5. Python ETL & Scripting Mastery#complete-production-ready-python-etl-script-example|2. ETL Architecture & Senior Gotchas]]\n- **Analogy:** 🌾 **Farm-to-Table Juice Factory** (Harvest raw fruit → Wash/peel/filter → Bottle in 1L glass).\n- **50GB Large Files (OOM Question):** Never use `file.read()`. Use **Generators with `yield`** (`for line in f:` streams line-by-line in **O(1) RAM**).\n- **Idempotency:** Write to staging partition first + atomic rename, or DB `UPSERT / ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE`.\n- **Error Handling:** Wrap record parsing in `try/except (ValueError, KeyError)`, route corrupt rows to DLQ, and keep the pipeline running.","x":-770,"y":-120,"width":700,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"argo_auth","type":"text","text":"### [[6. Argo CD Authentication & RBAC Mastery|1. Argo CD AuthN, SSO & Multi-Tenant RBAC]]\n- **Analogy:** 🛂 **Airport Immigration & Security Badging System**.\n- **Authentication (AuthN):** Disable local `admin` in `argocd-cm`. Implement **Direct OIDC SSO** with Microsoft Entra ID / Okta with corporate MFA.\n- **Authorization (AuthZ):** In `argocd-rbac-cm`, map OIDC groups to roles: `p, role:dev, applications, sync, project/*, allow`.\n- **AppProjects:** Physical tenant fence. Whitelists allowed Git repos, target clusters/namespaces, and blacklists `ClusterRoles`.","x":70,"y":-420,"width":700,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"argo_appsets","type":"text","text":"### [[7. Argo ApplicationSets vs. Argo Workflows|2. ApplicationSets vs. Argo Workflows]]\n- **ApplicationSets (Cookie-Cutter Mold):** Long-running declarative CD. Generators (`Git`, `Cluster`, `List`) scan repos and dynamically stamp out 50 apps across clusters.\n- **Argo Workflows (Rocket Launch DAG):** Finite batch execution. Steps run in ephemeral container pods in DAG order (DB migration → tests → cutover), exit with code 0, and stop.\n- **Pitch:** AppSets manage declarative multi-cluster state; Workflows orchestrate complex release verification before GitOps cutover.","x":70,"y":-120,"width":700,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"tf_arch","type":"text","text":"### [[8. Terraform Basics & Senior Q&A Mastery#the-analogy-the-architects-blueprint--the-city-land-registry|1. Core Architecture & State Management]]\n- **Analogy:** 🏗️ Blueprint (`*.tf`), Construction Site (Cloud), Land Registry (`tfstate`).\n- **State Locking:** GCS native atomic locking (or S3 + DynamoDB) prevents concurrent apply race conditions and state corruption.\n- **Directory-per-Env vs. Workspaces:** Workspaces share backend and blast radius! In production, use **Directory-per-Env (with Terragrunt)** for isolated state and IAM permissions.\n- **Layered State:** Layer 0 (IAM) → Layer 1 (VPC) → Layer 2 (GKE) → Layer 3 (Apps).","x":-770,"y":300,"width":440,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"tf_gotchas","type":"text","text":"### [[8. Terraform Basics & Senior Q&A Mastery#top-10-senior-terraform-interview-questions--answers|2. Senior Gotchas & Best Practices]]\n- **`for_each` vs `count`:** Never use `count` for lists! Removing index 0 triggers index shift that destroys and recreates subsequent resources. `for_each` uses stable string keys.\n- **Child Modules Rule:** **NEVER** put active `provider` blocks inside child modules. Root must pass providers down via aliases.\n- **`import` Block (TF 1.5+):** Declarative import with `-generate-config-out` writes HCL for PR review.\n- **GitOps for IaC:** Use Atlantis + Terragrunt for PR plan/apply audit trails.","x":-770,"y":600,"width":440,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"gcp_bridge","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#4-gcp-shared-vpc-vs-aws-transit-gateway--ram|1. AWS to GCP 1:1 Translation Bridge]]\n- **EKS IRSA** ↔ **GCP Workload Identity Federation (WIF)**: K8s ServiceAccount JWT exchanged via metadata server for temporary Google OAuth tokens (zero JSON keys).\n- **AWS Regional VPC + TGW** ↔ **GCP Global Shared VPC**: Central Host Project shares subnets directly to GKE Service Projects ($0 transit data fees, zero peering hops).\n- **PrivateLink** ↔ **Private Service Connect (PSC)**: Private unidirectional service endpoint; 100% immune to CIDR overlap collisions.","x":-230,"y":300,"width":460,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"platform_niche","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#1-capsule-kubernetes-multi-tenancy-operator|2. Core Platform Niche Stack Anchors]]\n- **Capsule (Multi-Tenancy):** High-rise leased floors. Tenant CRD, aggregate CPU/RAM quotas, regex Ingress & StorageClass whitelists.\n- **ARC on GKE:** Ephemeral runner pods scale on Spot nodes on demand and self-destruct after 1 build.\n- **Vault on K8s:** Dynamic DB credentials injected into in-memory `tmpfs` volumes via Vault Agent sidecar.\n- **Ansible for Windows:** Headless WinRM HTTPS for registry hardening & WSUS patching without interactive RDP.","x":-230,"y":600,"width":460,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sre_triage","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#11-production-incident-triage-sre--blameless-post-mortems|1. SRE Incident Triage (ER Trauma Team)]]\n- **Guiding Rule:** **\"Mitigate first, debug second\"** (customer SLA recovery is priority #1).\n- **Roles:** Incident Commander (stakeholder comms) vs. Technical Primaries (telemetry triage).\n- **MTTR Action:** Correlate with recent ArgoCD/Terraform releases; rollback commit or adjust scaling.\n- **Blameless Post-Mortem:** \"5 Whys\" root-cause analysis turned into automated prevention backlog tickets (e.g. Kyverno policy).","x":330,"y":300,"width":440,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"interview_closer","type":"text","text":"### [[2. Hiring Manager Prep & Strategy#part-6-high-signal-questions-to-ask-the-hiring-manager|2. Smart Questions to Ask the Manager]]\n1. *\"With RapidResponse operating across multiple clouds (GCP, Azure, AWS), how are you standardizing platform tooling across clusters?\"*\n2. *\"I saw that you use Capsule and self-hosted ARC runners on GKE. What does the developer self-service experience look like, and what is the biggest friction point today?\"*\n3. *\"What are the top 1–2 platform initiatives you want this Senior Engineer to own and deliver in the first 90 days?\"*","x":330,"y":600,"width":440,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"metrics_node","type":"text","text":"### ⚡ Your 5 Golden Resume Numbers\n1. **80%**: Compute cost cut (KEDA Scale-to-Zero on Spot)\n2. **8 Hours**: Manual release monitoring saved/cycle (Go engine)\n3. **2 Days → <10 Mins**: Sandbox provisioning lead time (Python bots)\n4. **5 AWS Accounts**: Centralized via Crossplane (3 days → 30m onboarding)\n5. **CAPA**: Certified Argo Project Associate (GitOps / AppSets)","x":120,"y":-740,"width":680,"height":200,"color":"4"}
	],
